  "result": "I found and fixed the bug. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:33` was matching cart lines by the item's name instead of its SKU:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.name != sku]\n```\n\nSo `remove('sku-1')` compared `'sku-1'` with the item name `'Widget'`. That never matched, and nothing was removed. I changed the comparison to `l.item.sku != sku`, which is also how `Cart.add` matches lines.\n\n**Results:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, so only the Gadget is left in the cart. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- All 6 existing tests pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\nNone of the tests call `Cart.remove`, which is why the suite didn't catch this. I haven't added a test for it; I can if you want one.",
